# 7. ARP Packet Analysis

ARP maps an IP address to a MAC address on a local network.

### Wireshark Filter

```text
arp
```

You may see:

```text
Who has 192.168.1.1?
Tell 192.168.1.10
```

Then:

```text
192.168.1.1 is at XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX
```

### ARP Mapping

```text
IP Address
    ↓
MAC Address
```

### SOC Perspective

ARP analysis can help identify:

* ARP spoofing
* Man-in-the-Middle attacks
* Rogue devices
* Duplicate IP/MAC relationships

Example suspicious behavior:

```text
Gateway IP
192.168.1.1
    |
    | Suddenly associated with
    v
Unknown / Attacker MAC Address
```

This could indicate ARP spoofing.

