# 9. Follow TCP Stream

Right-click a TCP packet:

```text
Right Click
    ↓
Follow
    ↓
TCP Stream
```

This reconstructs the communication between the client and server for that TCP session.

For unencrypted HTTP, you may be able to observe:

```text
GET /index.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: ...
```

For HTTPS, application data remains encrypted.

### SOC Use Cases

Follow TCP Stream helps analysts investigate:

* Client-server communication
* HTTP requests
* HTTP responses
* Suspicious payloads
* Potential malicious activity

