# 12. Packet Analysis Checklist

When investigating a packet or network connection, identify:

| Field            | Description                      |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Source IP        | Who sent the packet?             |
| Destination IP   | Who received the packet?         |
| Protocol         | TCP, UDP, DNS, HTTP, ICMP, etc.  |
| Source Port      | Source application port          |
| Destination Port | Target service port              |
| Packet Size      | Amount of data transferred       |
| Timestamp        | When the event occurred          |
| TCP Flags        | SYN, ACK, FIN, RST               |
| Domain           | Domain involved in communication |
| Action           | Normal or suspicious?            |

